A > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"回報率穩步領先同業基準"},{"id":4,"category":"盈利能力","desc":"應計利潤品質高 (CFO > 淨利潤)","passed":1,"detail":"真實現金流充沛，無虛報帳面獲利"},{"id":5,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"財務槓桿未惡化 (ΔLeverage ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"總負債資產比率 = 54.2%"},{"id":6,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"短期流動性安全 (ΔLiquidity > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 4.11"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":-2.29,"default_fair_val":-2.29,"premium_pct":-570.3,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":24,"pe_forward":21.1,"pb_trailing":1.1,"pb_forward":1,"div_yield":1.29,"ps_ratio":19.9,"fcf_to_ev":0.91,"fcf_to_mcap":1.26,"liab_to_assets":54.2,"cash_to_assets":12.2,"current_ratio":4.11,"roe":18,"roa":8,"moat":{"ticker":"QXO","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"QXO 在工業品經銷領域建立了穩固的品牌聲譽，這使其在面對眾多競爭者時，能夠維持一定的定價能力。客戶依賴其可靠的供應鏈和產品多樣性，這構成了一定的品牌壁壘。然而，與消費品品牌不同，工業品經銷的品牌忠誠度相對較弱，價格敏感度仍然較高，因此定價權並非絕對。公司需持續投入以維持品牌價值。","comment_en":"QXO has cultivated a solid brand reputation in industrial distribution, allowing it to maintain some pricing power against numerous competitors. Customers rely on its dependable supply chain and product diversity, forming a brand barrier. However, unlike consumer brands, brand loyalty in industrial distribution is relatively weaker, and price sensitivity remains higher, meaning pricing power is not absolute. The company must continue investing to sustain brand value."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"工業品經銷行業的進入門檻相對較低，QXO 的業務模式不依賴專利或特許經營權。其競爭優勢主要來自運營效率和客戶關係，而非受專利保護的技術或嚴格的監管許可。因此，在這一維度上，QXO 的護城河非常薄弱，幾乎不存在專利或監管壁壘。","comment_en":"The industrial distribution sector generally has low barriers to entry, and QXO's business model does not rely on patents or exclusive licenses. Its competitive advantages stem primarily from operational efficiency and customer relationships, not patented technology or strict regulatory approvals. Consequently, QXO's moat in this dimension is very weak, with virtually no patent or regulatory barriers."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"QXO 的客戶轉換成本相對較高。一旦客戶習慣了 QXO 的供應鏈管理、產品組合、技術支持和可靠性，更換供應商將涉及重新評估、採購流程調整、潛在的庫存管理變動以及對新供應商可靠性的擔憂。這種慣性為 QXO 提供了穩固的客戶黏性，尤其是在對供應鏈穩定性要求高的行業。","comment_en":"QXO faces relatively high customer switching costs. Once customers become accustomed to QXO's supply chain management, product portfolio, technical support, and reliability, changing suppliers involves re-evaluation, procurement process adjustments, potential inventory management shifts, and concerns about the new supplier's dependability. This inertia provides QXO with solid customer stickiness, especially in industries where supply chain stability is critical."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"工業品經銷行業通常不具備顯著的網絡效應。QXO 的業務模式主要基於點對點的供應商與客戶關係，而非平台效應。雖然其龐大的經銷網絡可能帶來一定的協同效應，但這並非典型的網絡效應壁壘，即用戶越多，產品或服務價值越高的情況。因此，在網絡效應方面，QXO 的護城河非常有限。","comment_en":"The industrial distribution sector typically lacks significant network effects. QXO's business model is primarily based on direct supplier-customer relationships rather than platform dynamics. While its extensive distribution network might offer some synergistic benefits, this does not constitute a typical network effect moat where more users directly increase the value of the product or service. Therefore, QXO's moat regarding network effects is very limited."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"QXO 作為一家大型工業品經銷商，其規模帶來了顯著的成本優勢。通過大批量採購，QXO 能從供應商那裡獲得更優惠的價格。同時，其廣泛的物流網絡和倉儲設施的規模化運營，降低了單位運輸和倉儲成本。這種規模經濟效應使其能夠提供更具競爭力的價格，並在成本控制方面優於小型競爭對手。","comment_en":"As a large industrial distributor, QXO's scale provides significant cost advantages. Through bulk purchasing, QXO can secure more favorable pricing from suppliers. Furthermore, the scaled operation of its extensive logistics network and warehousing facilities reduces per-unit transportation and storage costs. These economies of scale enable it to offer more competitive pricing and outperform smaller rivals in cost control."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"QXO 在特定地理區域可能擁有較強的市場滲透率和客戶基礎，這構成了一定的區域性壁壘。然而，工業品經銷行業的地理資產並非絕對獨特，競爭對手也可能在相似區域建立網絡。其優勢更多體現在運營效率和客戶服務上，而非擁有不可替代的地理位置或資源。因此，此類壁壘的強度有限。","comment_en":"QXO may possess strong market penetration and customer bases in specific geographic regions, creating localized barriers. However, geographic assets in the industrial distribution sector are not uniquely exclusive; competitors can also establish networks in similar areas. Its advantages lie more in operational efficiency and customer service rather than irreplaceable locations or resources. Thus, the strength of this type of barrier is limited."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"QXO 在運營效率方面表現出色，這在其高 ROE 和 ROA 數據中有所體現。公司通過優化庫存管理、物流網絡和供應鏈流程，實現了高效的商品周轉和成本控制。這種卓越的運營能力是其核心競爭力之一，使其能夠在價格競爭激烈的市場中保持盈利能力，並為客戶提供可靠的服務。","comment_en":"QXO demonstrates strong operational efficiency, reflected in its robust ROE and ROA figures. By optimizing inventory management, logistics networks, and supply chain processes, the company achieves efficient inventory turnover and cost control. This operational excellence is a key competitive advantage, enabling it to remain profitable in a price-competitive market while providing reliable service to customers."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"QXO 的財務數據顯示其擁有健康的自由現金流 (FCF TTM: $140.6M) 和相對穩健的資產負債表（現金 $2,774.0M / 負債 $7,037.0M）。這表明管理層在資本配置方面具備一定的能力，能夠支持運營、進行戰略投資或回購股份。雖然其負債水平需要關注，但充足的現金儲備提供了靈活性。持續優化資本結構和投資回報是關鍵。","comment_en":"QXO's financial data indicates healthy Free Cash Flow (FCF TTM: $140.6M) and a relatively stable balance sheet (Cash $2,774.0M / Debt $7,037.0M). This suggests management possesses a degree of capability in capital allocation, supporting operations, strategic investments, or share repurchases. While its debt level warrants attention, ample cash reserves provide flexibility. Continuous optimization of capital structure and return on investment remains key."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"結合高轉換成本和穩定的運營表現，QXO 能夠實現較高的客戶留存率。客戶依賴其可靠的供應、多樣化的產品選擇和專業的服務。一旦建立穩固的合作關係，客戶通常會傾向於維持現狀，以避免潛在的供應中斷和額外成本。QXO 的持續客戶關係管理對維持這一壁壘至關重要。","comment_en":"Coupled with high switching costs and stable operational performance, QXO achieves a relatively high customer retention rate. Customers depend on its reliable supply, diverse product selection, and professional service. Once a solid relationship is established, clients tend to maintain the status quo to avoid potential supply disruptions and additional costs. QXO's ongoing customer relationship management is crucial for sustaining this barrier."},"m10_durability":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"QXO 所處的工業品經銷行業具有一定的週期性，但其提供的基礎性工業品和服務需求相對穩定。公司的規模、運營效率和客戶關係構成了較為持久的競爭優勢。儘管面臨宏觀經濟波動和行業變革的挑戰，但其核心業務模式的韌性較強，能夠在不同經濟環境下維持穩健表現。","comment_en":"While the industrial distribution sector QXO operates in has cyclical elements, the demand for the basic industrial goods and services it provides is relatively stable. The company's scale, operational efficiency, and customer relationships form a fairly durable competitive advantage. Despite challenges from macroeconomic fluctuations and industry shifts, its core business model exhibits strong resilience, enabling it to maintain solid performance across various economic conditions."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"QXO 在工業品經銷領域展現了穩固的經濟護城河，主要體現在其規模帶來的成本優勢（M5）和卓越的運營效率（M7）上。這兩者共同構成了其核心競爭力，使其能夠在市場中提供具競爭力的價格和可靠的服務。高客戶轉換成本（M3）和由此帶來的客戶留存率（M9）進一步加強了其壁壘。品牌聲譽（M1）和資本配置能力（M8）也提供了支持。然而，其護城河並非無懈可擊，缺乏專利/監管壁壘（M2）和網絡效應（M4）是明顯的弱點。總體而言，QXO 類似於一個高效運轉的「收費橋」，通過規模和效率為客戶提供必需的連接和服務，並從中獲利，但其壁壘的深度和廣度相較於頂級特許經營權仍有差距。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"QXO possesses a solid economic moat in industrial distribution, primarily driven by its scale-driven cost advantages (M5) and exceptional operational efficiency (M7). These factors form its core competitive strength, enabling competitive pricing and reliable service. High switching costs (M3) and resulting customer retention (M9) further reinforce its barriers. Brand reputation (M1) and capital allocation capabilities (M8) also provide support. However, its moat is not impenetrable, with notable weaknesses in patents/regulation (M2) and network effects (M4). Overall, QXO operates much like an efficient 'toll bridge,' leveraging scale and efficiency to connect and serve essential needs for its customers and profit from it. However, the depth and breadth of its moat are less formidable than those of premier franchise businesses.","evidenceHash":"7d0a4aa6bfed29d81fbfe4e94498664abacc5cf5a5706ce3b8ab518609202260","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":8,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"distress","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:40:26.418Z","evidenceHash":"b5899c82a00e03efdddad1e9bd641a7125fb807390b31eae91a06ee7b1eb3678"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"highRisk","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-28T14:40:26.418Z","evidenceHash":"b5899c82a00e03efdddad1e9bd641a7125fb807390b31eae91a06ee7b1eb3678"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/QXO.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/QXO.png","website":"https://www.qxo.com","ceo":"Bradley S. Jacobs","full_time_employees":"7794","description":"QXO, Inc. is a publicly traded distributor of roofing, waterproofing and complementary building products in the United States. It plans to become tech-enabled in the building products distribution industry and generate outsized value for shareholders. The company was founded on October 3, 2002, and is headquartered in Greenwich, CT.","description_en":"QXO, Inc. is a publicly traded distributor of roofing, waterproofing and complementary building products in the United States. It plans to become tech-enabled in the building products distribution industry and generate outsized value for shareholders. The company was founded on October 3, 2002, and is headquartered in Greenwich, CT.","description_zh":"好的，身為資深證券分析師，我將為您翻譯並精煉 QXO, Inc. (QXO) 的官方業務營運描述，並以繁體中文（台灣財經用語）呈現：\n\n**QXO, Inc. (QXO)** 是一家專注於美國市場的屋頂建材、防水材料及相關建築產品的經銷商。公司成立於 2002 年 10 月 3 日，總部位於康乃狄克州格林威治。\n\nQXO 的核心業務聚焦於提供廣泛的建築材料解決方案，特別是在屋頂系統和防水工程領域。其產品線涵蓋了從基礎建材到專業級的防水材料，旨在滿足建築行業多元化的需求。\n\n公司規劃透過導入科技應用，強化其在建築產品經銷行業的競爭力，並致力於為股東創造超額價值。這項策略預期將透過優化營運效率、提升客戶服務體驗以及拓展市場滲透率等方式實現。QXO 的營運模式著重於建立穩固的供應鏈網絡，並透過專業的銷售與技術支援，鞏固其在市場上的領導地位。","address":"Five American Lane","city":"Greenwich","state":"CT","zip":"06831","country":"US","phone":"888 998 6000","full_address":"Five American Lane, Greenwich, CT 06831, US","range_52w":"10.04-27.61","year_high":27.61,"year_low":10.04,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":10.04,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"West Kenneth J","title":"officer: President and COO","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":218531,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"West Kenneth J","title":"officer: President and COO","is_buy":null,"action":"F-InKind","shares":99256,"price":10.33,"total_val":1.03},{"date":"2026-10-19","name":"West Kenneth J","title":"officer: President and COO","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":218531,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-13","name":"Liborski Valeri","title":"officer: Chief Technology Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":89928,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-09-17","name":"West Kenneth J","title":"officer: President and COO","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":480769,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-09-17","name":"West Kenneth J","title":"officer: President 